From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:52:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] AMLDisplay: write CRTC properties as non-blocking requests

Each Dolby Vision property was written as its own blocking commit. The
kernel applies the value when it parses the ioctl, but the commit
still waits for a vblank. The five to six writes at a DV open block
the player for 217 to 290 ms before the decoder starts, and the close
writes cost about as much again.
